**Incident Ticket #INC-4921 — DHCP Service Degradation (Data Center)**

**Severity:** P2  
**Service:** DHCP for DC edge fabric  
**Impact:** Intermittent lease failures for bare-metal hosts in VLAN 110 (build subnet 10.11.10.0/24). Clients report “No offer received” during PXE boot, while existing leases renew fine. DHCP server load is low.

**Environment:** Single Kea DHCP server (v2.x) with dual network interfaces. It uses a config file loaded at startup. The server forwards DNS resolver information to clients. Recent change: an operator added a new subnet definition for VLAN 120 (10.11.20.0/24) to support a staging environment, then reloaded the server.

**Configuration excerpt (supplied for review):**

```
"subnet4": [
  {
    "subnet": "10.11.10.0/24",
    "id": 110,
    "pools": [ { "pool": "10.11.10.100 - 10.11.10.200" } ],
    "option-data": [
      { "name": "routers", "data": "10.11.10.1" },
      { "name": "domain-name-servers", "data": "10.11.9.53, 10.11.9.54" }
    ],
    "reservations": [
      { "hw-address": "aa:bb:cc:dd:ee:01", "ip-address": "10.11.10.50" }
    ]
  },
  {
    "subnet": "10.11.20.0/24",
    "id": 120,
    "pools": [ { "pool": "10.11.20.100 - 10.11.20.200" } ],
    "option-data": [
      { "name": "routers", "data": "10.11.20.1" },
      { "name": "domain-name-servers", "data": "10.11.9.53, 10.11.9.54" }
